llot."]}, "overview": "Nevada's 2nd District is an open Republican-held seat with a strong R+7 partisan lean, and most expert raters call it Likely R, though two say Lean R. Republican David Flippo has heavily outraised Democrat Teresa Benitez-Thompson and holds a large outside-spending edge, and prediction markets give Republicans roughly a three-in-four chance.\n\nStill, the race has drawn unusual attention: Flippo faces reports about a disputed Bronze Star claim, carpetbagger allegations, and ads from Nevada veterans opposing him, while Benitez-Thompson has gained national Democratic backing. Limited polling from late summer showed a near-even contest, though the samples are small and dated. The evidence points to a Republican lean rather than a safe seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.213, "margin": -4.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2977, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2868, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2952, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2127, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2908, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3508, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3896, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3448, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3118, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2576, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2807, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1915, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2968, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3004, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2172, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2027, "margin": -5.0}]}